<title>THAILAND: KR Precision takes $25 million loan.</title>
<headline>KR Precision takes $25 million loan.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai precision component manufacturer KR Precision Plc said on Monday it has signed a $25 million syndicated loan agreement to finance factory expansion.</p>
<p>The three year loan costs 1.25 percent over SIBOR and is repayable in three annual installments, a company statement said.</p>
<p>Lenders include Sakura Bank Ltd, The Long-Term Credit Bank of Japan Ltd, Sanwa Bank Ltd and Sumitomo Bank Ltd, the company said.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
